{
 "title": "Why are clouds white when the sky is blue",
 "sentences": [
  {
   "n": 1,
   "display": "Why are clouds white… when the sky is blue?",
   "pauseBefore": null,
   "title": true,
   "start": 0.08,
   "end": 3.25,
   "marks": [
    [
     3,
     1.68,
     1.94
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 2,
   "display": "Same sunlight.",
   "pauseBefore": null,
   "start": 3.72,
   "end": 4.56
  },
  {
   "n": 3,
   "display": "Same air.",
   "pauseBefore": null,
   "start": 4.78,
   "end": 5.62
  },
  {
   "n": 4,
   "display": "Totally DIFFERENT colour.",
   "pauseBefore": null,
   "start": 5.94,
   "end": 7.23
  },
  {
   "n": 5,
   "display": "Here's what's actually happening.",
   "pauseBefore": null,
   "start": 7.7,
   "end": 9.24
  },
  {
   "n": 6,
   "display": "A cloud is made of billions of tiny water droplets.",
   "pauseBefore": null,
   "start": 9.63,
   "end": 12.91
  },
  {
   "n": 7,
   "display": "Air molecules are so small, they mostly scatter blue light.",
   "pauseBefore": null,
   "start": 13.3,
   "end": 16.9
  },
  {
   "n": 8,
   "display": "That's why the sky is blue.",
   "pauseBefore": null,
   "start": 17.23,
   "end": 18.53
  },
  {
   "n": 9,
   "display": "But cloud droplets are HUGE compared to light waves.",
   "pauseBefore": null,
   "start": 18.93,
   "end": 21.88
  },
  {
   "n": 10,
   "display": "So they scatter every colour… *equally*.",
   "pauseBefore": null,
   "start": 22.12,
   "end": 24.48,
   "marks": [
    [
     4,
     22.89,
     23.02
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 11,
   "display": "Red.",
   "pauseBefore": null,
   "start": 24.89,
   "end": 25.33
  },
  {
   "n": 12,
   "display": "Green.",
   "pauseBefore": null,
   "start": 25.61,
   "end": 26.08
  },
  {
   "n": 13,
   "display": "Blue.",
   "pauseBefore": null,
   "start": 26.31,
   "end": 26.65
  },
  {
   "n": 14,
   "display": "All bounced back together.",
   "pauseBefore": null,
   "start": 26.98,
   "end": 28.35
  },
  {
   "n": 15,
   "display": "And every colour mixed together… is WHITE.",
   "pauseBefore": null,
   "start": 28.69,
   "end": 31.16,
   "marks": [
    [
     4,
     30.34,
     30.59
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 16,
   "display": "That's called MIE SCATTERING.",
   "pauseBefore": null,
   "concept": true,
   "start": 31.54,
   "end": 33.12
  },
  {
   "n": 17,
   "display": "Now look at a storm cloud.",
   "pauseBefore": null,
   "start": 33.55,
   "end": 34.91
  },
  {
   "n": 18,
   "display": "Same water.",
   "pauseBefore": null,
   "start": 35.24,
   "end": 36.03
  },
  {
   "n": 19,
   "display": "Same droplets.",
   "pauseBefore": null,
   "start": 36.19,
   "end": 37.18
  },
  {
   "n": 20,
   "display": "So why is it GREY?",
   "pauseBefore": null,
   "start": 37.47,
   "end": 38.87
  },
  {
   "n": 21,
   "display": "Because it's so thick, most of the light gets scattered back out of the top… before it ever reaches the bottom.",
   "pauseBefore": null,
   "start": 39.3,
   "end": 45.12,
   "marks": [
    [
     3,
     40.62,
     40.79
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "n": 22,
   "display": "You're not seeing a dark cloud.",
   "pauseBefore": null,
   "start": 45.56,
   "end": 47.23
  },
  {
   "n": 23,
   "display": "You're seeing a cloud that ran out of *light*.",
   "pauseBefore": null,
   "start": 47.66,
   "end": 49.84
  },
  {
   "n": 24,
   "display": "So next time someone asks why clouds are white… you'll know.",
   "pauseBefore": null,
   "start": 50.21,
   "end": 53.56,
